#
# === #53 bilateral pair with docblock_no_extraction_pattern (recognition #53) ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]` (recognition
# #53): declarative property at
# `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` + operational fracture body
# at `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>`, bridged by the kintsugi
# loop. THIS SHARD is the operational half of the sixth #53
# family's third-of-trio predicate:
# `docblock_no_extraction_pattern` (declarative half at TICK 7
# `c56c3c8`, Seam RATIFY `1f8df3f`).
#
# Prior five #53 instances (per docblock_no_extraction_pattern
# shard's own ancestor tally):
#
# 1. `@kintsugi/fracture/keyword` (2026-06-10 `d908798`) — first.
# 2. `@mirror/fracture/predicate` (task #272 forward-promised).
# 3. `dark_count_monotone` (2026-06-19 `499ffd9`) — third.
# 4. `cold_compile_within_tolerance` (2026-06-19) — fourth.
# 5. `@kintsugi/surface` + `ashby_variety_match` (2026-07-03
#    `e910dd6`) — fifth.
#
# Sixth family's first operational half landed TICK 4 as
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded` (Seam RATIFY `9b0aeb5`);
# sixth family's second operational half landed TICK 6 as
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent` (Seam RATIFY `caab92f`).
# THIS is the sixth family's THIRD-of-trio operational half, paired
# with `docblock_no_extraction_pattern` (declarative half at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/docblock_no_extraction_pattern.mirror`,
# TICK 7 GREEN `c56c3c8`, Seam RATIFY `1f8df3f`). The declarative
# side names WHAT it means for a docblock to be free of the four
# extractive shapes; THIS operational side names WHAT TO DO when
# the docblock's claims exhibit any of those shapes — routing
# THREE-WAY per sub-check across `@kintsugi/surface`'s classes
# plus a fourth deterministic path via
# `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` kind-reclassification.
#
# === Operational role: fracture body of extraction-pattern audit ===
#
# When `docblock_no_extraction_pattern(d)` returns a failure verdict
# — one or more of the four sub-checks unbounded per Mara spec
# §7 — this fracture body's action fires. The body's discharge
# shape depends on WHICH sub-check fired:
#
#   sub-check 1 unbounded (no_unmarked_superlatives)
#     ⇒ kintsugi_lock_of(d, ctx) fires `ashby_mismatch`
#     ⇒ surface(d, ashby_mismatch, ctx) emits Tomm-circular
#       question at reader-frame altitude naming which
#       variety-axis the doc-side over-claims relative to the
#       code-side landing
#     ⇒ observation_depth returned as third-order witness
#
#   sub-check 3 unbounded (citations_content_match)
#     ⇒ kintsugi_lock_of(d, ctx) fires `out_of_band`
#     ⇒ surface(d, out_of_band, ctx) emits Tomm-strategic
#       question at reader-frame altitude naming which
#       namespace-frame the citation opens that the substrate
#       cannot bind at the claim's grounding altitude
#     ⇒ observation_depth returned as third-order witness
#
#   sub-check 4 unbounded (claim_size_matches_landing_size)
#     ⇒ kintsugi_lock_of(d, ctx) fires `contradiction`
#     ⇒ surface(d, contradiction, ctx) emits Tomm-reflexive
#       question at reader-frame altitude naming the scope-
#       arithmetic mismatch: the claim's implicit universal
#       fires success on a landing that witnesses only a proper
#       subset
#     ⇒ observation_depth returned as third-order witness
#
#   sub-check 2 unbounded (hedged_claims_marked_defer)
#     ⇒ kind-reclassification path via
#       `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` — the extractor
#       rewrites the claim's `kind` field from unmarked hedge
#       to `forward_promise` with a `defer` marker and closure
#       tick, deterministically. NO reader-frame surfacing;
#       the fix is mechanical per Mara spec §8.
#
# The body is bilateral to `docblock_no_extraction_pattern`: the
# predicate's failure IS this body's activation site; this body's
# discharge closes the loop back to the predicate at the next
# kintsugi tick. No manual patching; no opaque carrier substitution;
# the closure rides either `@kintsugi/surface`'s spawn branch
# (sub-checks 1, 3, 4) or `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction`'s
# rewrite branch (sub-check 2) per
# `[[feedback-manual-closure-is-training-pull]]`.
#
# === Three-way routing across surface classes (compiler-error-surface §3) ===
#
# The three sub-checks that surface via `@kintsugi/surface`
# specialize distinct routing arms:
#
# Sub-check 1 → `ashby_mismatch` (compiler-error-surface §3.1):
# per Ashby (1956) *Introduction to Cybernetics* §11's variety-
# attenuation ladder — the doc-side claims more variety than the
# code-side landing can absorb; V(D_doc) > V(R_code) on the
# axis the superlative names. Tomm shape (§5.2): circular — the
# question loops the observer through which variety-axis the
# doc side over-claims rather than declaring a linear fix.
# Ashby-mismatch rigor per §4.1 rigor table: MOTIVATING pending
# per-class projection-operator derivation on `𝔤 → 𝔤_variety-
# axis-N`.
#
# Sub-check 3 → `out_of_band` (compiler-error-surface §3.4):
# per `error-as-question.md` §4 (algedonic bypass) — the
# citation opens a namespace the substrate cannot bind at the
# frame the claim needs; the substrate's `A` (algebra at
# reader-frame altitude) does not contain the citation's
# `namespace_requested`. Tomm shape (§5.5): strategic — the
# question directs the observer toward which FUTURE of the
# substrate should be taken (widen the algebra? retract the
# claim? move the citation?). Out-of-band rigor per §4.1
# rigor table: MOTIVATING pending per-class projection-operator
# derivation on `𝔤 → 𝔤_algebra-membership`.
#
# Sub-check 4 → `contradiction` (compiler-error-surface §3.2):
# per Carnielli-Marcos LFI (2004, 2007) — the doc-side claim
# and the code-side landing contradict at scope-arithmetic
# altitude; the claim's implicit universal quantifier fires
# success while the landing witnesses only a proper subset of
# what the claim covers. Tomm shape (§5.4): reflexive — the
# question folds the observer back onto the scope arithmetic
# itself: "what does my claim-size vs landing-size ratio say
# about the substrate's local geometry?" Contradiction is
# THE ONE RIGOROUS surface class of the four per §4.1 rigor
# table: its projection operator is DERIVED from the curvature
# 2-form `Ω = dω + ½[ω, ω]` — the `[ω, ω]` Bateson-bind
# IS the bracket term.
#
# === Kind-reclassification path via @epistemologic/liquid_extraction (sub-check 2) ===
#
# Sub-check 2 (`hedged_claims_marked_defer`) does NOT route to
# `@kintsugi/surface`. Per Mara spec §8: unmarked hedges are
# mechanically decidable — the fix is a `kind`-field rewrite
# from `grounded_claim` or `candidate_claim` (whichever the
# extractor initially assigned) to `forward_promise` with a
# `defer` marker naming the closure tick. This is a
# DETERMINISTIC path via the sibling family-root
# `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` (TICK 2 RATIFY `3283de4`):
# the extractor's `extract_predicate` re-emits the doc_claim
# with the kind reclassified. NO reader-frame surfacing; the
# kintsugi loop closes at extractor altitude without a Tomm
# question because there IS no unresolved observer-frame
# question — the hedge IS the substrate's uncertainty naming
# itself, and the required response is deterministic marker
# insertion.
#
# This three-way-plus-one routing is the substrate's first
# operational instance of a fracture body that fires FOUR
# distinct kintsugi discharges per Mara spec §8. The trio's
# first two bilaterals routed one-way (docblock_ungrounded
# → ashby_mismatch; docblock_incoherent → contradiction);
# THIS bilateral is the first to route three-way on the surface
# side and to add a fourth deterministic-rewrite path.
# Bilateral pattern #53 absorbs this variance without new
# structural primitives — the fracture body is still a single
# `@kintsugi/fracture/*` action; the routing surface at
# `@kintsugi/surface` still names each class; the substrate's
# `ashby_variety_match` still discharges each dispatch; the
# `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` sibling family-root
# absorbs the deterministic rewrite path already exported
# from TICK 2.
#
# === Twelfth-instance discipline via ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock) ===
#
# The `requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` clause on
# this fracture body IS the twelfth-instance discipline per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`: the substrate
# had `ashby_variety_match(lock: lock_carrier) -> verdict`
# landed at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.mirror`.
# We consume the landed ancestor; we do not invent a new
# predicate at doc-claim altitude. Same routing gate as
# `@kintsugi/surface.surface(...)`,
# `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm.resolve_restart_storm(...)`,
# TICK 4's `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded.
# docblock_ungrounded_body(...)` (Seam RATIFY `9b0aeb5`),
# and TICK 6's `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent.
# docblock_incoherent_body(...)` (Seam RATIFY `caab92f`).
# The eleventh instance (docblock_incoherent) preceded this
# landing by exactly two ticks in the trio; this is the
# twelfth consecutive discharge through the same landed
# ancestor across the substrate's fracture-body ladder, and
# THE landed instance that closes sub-arc A.
#
# === Sub-arc A closure recognition ===
#
# Per Mara spec `docs/specs/doc-code-seam-shards.md` §Landing
# order: the sixth #53 family is expressed as three
# property/fracture bilateral pairs across TICKs 3-8. The
# first two pairs completed at TICK 4 (docblock_grounded /
# docblock_ungrounded, Seam RATIFY `ff53d46` / `9b0aeb5`)
# and TICK 6 (docblock_coherent / docblock_incoherent,
# Seam RATIFY `83bbdc8` / `caab92f`). THIS landing is the
# GREEN of the third-of-trio operational half; Seam RATIFY
# at Phase D closes the third pair and thereby closes
# sub-arc A. The trio's declarative-side second-witness
# audits (TICK 3 → TICK 5, TICK 5 → TICK 7, TICK 7 → THIS
# TICK's Seam Phase D) chain into the sub-arc's closure
# discipline: three independent property/fracture pairs at
# a shared family altitude constitute the sixth #53 family;
# the sixth family's own second-witness discipline promotes
# recognition #53 itself per the property-fracture bilateral
# instance count.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/docblock_extractive.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_extractive` at species-depth 2
# under @kintsugi per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. Same depth as
# the twelve landed sibling fracture bodies
# (`shards/kintsugi/fracture/{keyword,angle_to_paren,symbol_lift,
# operator_match,dark_count_monotone,cold_compile_within_tolerance,
# gate,partials_align,parent_cycle,restart_storm,
# docblock_ungrounded,docblock_incoherent}.mirror`); this shard
# sits in the same species column and is subject to the same
# path-namespace pact. Sibling declarative half at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/docblock_no_extraction_pattern.mirror`
# (`@epistemologic/property/docblock_no_extraction_pattern`,
# species-depth 2 under @epistemologic) — bilateral coupling
# honours the family/species partition per
# `[[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]`:
# form-side under @epistemologic; process-side under @kintsugi.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per Mara's projection-surface spec `63bdecc` §6 the operator
# must audit its own audit at depth=3. THIS shard's own docblock
# is subject to `docblock_no_extraction_pattern(this_docblock)`
# at logical altitude — the exact predicate whose failure this
# shard's body routes. Substrate-honest verdict at THIS shard's
# state on all four sub-checks:
#
# - Sub-check 1 (`no_unmarked_superlatives`): the narrative
#   above uses "load-bearing", "canonical", and "first" — each
#   in a substrate-honoring frame. "Load-bearing action" names
#   the substrate's own load-bearing discipline; "Interpretation
#   B canonical" cites the Seam pre-review document that ratifies
#   the discipline; "first operational instance of a fracture
#   body that fires FOUR distinct kintsugi discharges" names a
#   factual first grounded by the two prior one-way-routing
#   bilaterals (TICK 4, TICK 6) — a count, not a superlative
#   on quality. "THE ONE RIGOROUS surface class of the four"
#   is a direct quote from compiler-error-surface §4.1's rigor
#   table (grounded verbatim). No unmarked superlative fires at
#   analytical altitude.
#
# - Sub-check 2 (`hedged_claims_marked_defer`): the narrative
#   hedges on empirical composition ("cannot yet concretely
#   discharge", "concrete byte-match awaits the extractor body");
#   each hedge is anchored to the forward-promise on the
#   extractor body (TICK 2 sibling family-root's
#   `extract_predicate` action, currently `\`-obligated per
#   the substrate's forward-promise honor). The `defer` marker
#   is the forward-promise itself per @docblock's carrier
#   surface. No unmarked hedge fires.
#
# - Sub-check 3 (`citations_content_match`): the narrative cites
#   eight ratification commits (`820a451`, `3283de4`, `ff53d46`,
#   `9b0aeb5`, `83bbdc8`, `caab92f`, `1f8df3f`, and GREEN
#   `c56c3c8`), prior #53 instance commits (`d908798`,
#   `499ffd9`, `e910dd6`), plus substrate document paths (Mara
#   spec §7, §8; compiler-error-surface §3.1, §3.2, §3.4,
#   §4.1, §5.2, §5.4, §5.5; projection-surface §6; error-as-
#   question §4; Seam pre-review §1). Each citation resolves
#   to an ancestor on main; each ancestor's content grounds
#   the claim it appears in at the frame the claim needs.
#   Concrete byte-match awaits the extractor body (TICK 2
#   forward-promise).
#
# - Sub-check 4 (`claim_size_matches_landing_size`): the
#   narrative makes claims at three scopes: (i) claims about
#   THIS shard's below-seam declarations (the glass block and
#   fracture body signature); (ii) claims about the trio's
#   internal ordering (grounded by the seven preceding
#   ratification commits including TICK 7); (iii) claims about
#   the sixth #53 family membership (grounded by the five
#   prior family instances). Each claim's scope matches its
#   landing size: (i) matches the below-seam glass + fracture
#   body; (ii) matches the seven Seam ratification commits;
#   (iii) matches the five prior family citations. No claim
#   exceeds its landing.
#
# Verdict: `both_survive` — the shard's docblock passes real
# survival on all four sub-checks at analytical altitude but
# phantom survival is also non-empty (the extractor body has
# not landed; concrete byte-match on citations cannot fire
# until it does; the three-way routing has not been exercised
# against a live doc_claim carrying any of the four extractive
# shapes; empirical composition witness across the four
# discharge paths is deferred per
# `[[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]]`).
# Promotion to `real_survives` awaits: extractor body (TICK 2
# forward-promise) + Seam second-witness audit on this shard's
# routing arms + empirical composition against a runtime
# kintsugi tick firing each of the four discharge paths. Per
# Mara spec §Cross-cutting: this is the substrate-honest
# verdict at THIS shard's state. Substrate-pull chose
# `both_survive` over a performed `real_survives` — the
# fracture body cannot yet concretely discharge, and honoring
# that gap is the discipline that closes sub-arc A honestly.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/ashby-1956
source @arxiv/logic/carnielli-marcos-2004

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi
in @kintsugi/surface
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @epistemologic/property/docblock_no_extraction_pattern
in @epistemologic/liquid_extraction
in @docblock

glass @kintsugi/fracture/docblock_extractive {
  focus fracture_body
  project fracture_body
  split fracture_body
  shift fracture_body
  settle fracture_body
}

# === docblock_extractive_body (fracture body; operational half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Reads a `docblock` d whose
# `docblock_no_extraction_pattern` verdict fired failure on one
# or more of the four sub-checks, and a `kintsugi_context` ctx
# from the enclosing loop. Routes FOUR-WAY per sub-check per
# Mara spec §8:
#
#   sub-check 1 (no_unmarked_superlatives) →
#     surface(d, ashby_mismatch, ctx)   — Tomm circular    (§5.2)
#   sub-check 3 (citations_content_match) →
#     surface(d, out_of_band, ctx)      — Tomm strategic   (§5.5)
#   sub-check 4 (claim_size_matches_landing_size) →
#     surface(d, contradiction, ctx)    — Tomm reflexive   (§5.4)
#   sub-check 2 (hedged_claims_marked_defer) →
#     @epistemologic/liquid_extraction  — kind-reclassification
#                                         (deterministic; no
#                                          reader-frame surfacing)
#
# Three of the four discharges emit a Tomm-shaped question at
# reader-frame altitude via `@kintsugi/surface`'s three-mode-
# algebra spawn branch (spec §7.2 canonical signature) and
# return an `observation_depth` witness. The fourth (sub-check
# 2) discharges deterministically through the sibling family-
# root `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction`'s `extract_predicate`
# rewrite — no observation depth is required because there is
# no unresolved observer-frame question at that discharge.
#
# The `requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` clause
# honours the twelfth-instance discipline per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`: same landed
# ancestor at `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric`
# consumed by `@kintsugi/surface.surface(...)`,
# `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm.resolve_restart_storm(...)`,
# TICK 4's `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded.
# docblock_ungrounded_body(...)`, and TICK 6's
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent.
# docblock_incoherent_body(...)`.
#
# Body forward-promised per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`;
# discharge composes over the four routing arms at the `\`
# obligation site when the extractor body (TICK 2 forward-
# promise `extract_predicate`) lands and a live docblock fires
# any of the four sub-checks. This IS the third-of-trio
# operational half; its Seam RATIFY closes sub-arc A.
docblock_extractive_body(d: docblock, ctx: kintsugi_context) -> ref
  requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)
{ \ }

out @kintsugi/fracture/docblock_extractive
out docblock_extractive_body
